    "total_in_level": 10,
    "title": "Advanced Pronouns",
    "subtitle": "double object pronouns, placement, redundant pronouns, verbs like gustar, neutral lo, prepositional pronouns, leísmo",
    "footer": "Spanish Learning Program · B2 · Grammar · Advanced pronouns",
    "next": "Next: B2 · PDF 8 — Emphasis, word order and suffixes"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "After this PDF you can",
      "bullets": [
        "combine two object pronouns (se lo, me lo, te la) in the right order",
        "place pronouns with infinitives, gerunds, imperatives and periphrases",
        "use redundant pronouns (A mí me gusta, Le di el libro a Ana)",
        "use the neutral lo (lo bueno, lo que, lo de) and prepositional pronouns (conmigo, entre tú y yo)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "1. Double object pronouns"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Order: <b>indirect (me, te, le, nos, os, les) + direct (lo, la, los, las)</b>. Indirect before direct, both before the verb."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        5.6,
        5.8,
        5.6
      ],
      "head": [
        "Sentence",
        "With pronouns",
        "English"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Doy el libro a ti.",
          "Te lo doy.",
          "I give it to you."
        ],
        [
          "Mandó la carta a nosotros.",
          "Nos la mandó.",
          "He sent it to us."
        ],
        [
          "Explicaré las reglas a vosotros.",
          "Os las explicaré.",
          "I will explain them to you."
        ],
        [
          "Dije la verdad a Ana.",
          "Se la dije.",
          "I told it to her."
        ],
        [
          "Compré flores a mis padres.",
          "Se las compré.",
          "I bought them for them."
        ],
        [
          "Presté mi coche a él.",
          "Se lo presté.",
          "I lent it to him."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "warn",
      "title": "le / les + lo = se lo",
      "text": "When <b>le</b> or <b>les</b> comes before <b>lo, la, los, las</b>, it becomes <b>se</b>: <i>Le doy el libro</i> gives <i>Se lo doy</i>, never <i>Le lo doy</i>. To make it clear who, add <b>a él / a ella / a usted / a ellos</b>: <i>Se lo doy a ella.</i>"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Placement"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        5.0,
        6.2,
        5.8
      ],
      "head": [
        "Verb form",
        "Example",
        "Rule"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Finite verb",
          "Me lo dijo.",
          "before the verb"
        ],
        [
          "Infinitive",
          "Voy a decírtelo. / Te lo voy a decir.",
          "after (attached) or before auxiliary"
        ],
        [
          "Gerund",
          "Estoy explicándotelo. / Te lo estoy explicando.",
          "after (attached) or before auxiliary"
        ],
        [
          "Positive imperative",
          "Dímelo. / Dáselo.",
          "after, attached"
        ],
        [
          "Negative imperative",
          "No me lo digas. / No se lo des.",
          "before the verb"
        ],
        [
          "Compound tense",
          "Me lo ha dicho.",
          "before haber, never between"
        ],
        [
          "Perfect gerund",
          "Habiéndotelo dicho, me fui.",
          "attached to habiendo"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "<b>Written accents</b> keep stress when pronouns are added: <i>dime, dímelo, dándoselo, escríbemelo</i>.",
        "<b>Reflexive + object:</b> <i>Me lo pongo. Se lo quitó.</i> (the reflexive comes first: se, me, te, nos, os).",
        "In the positive imperative with nosotros, drop the -s of the verb before <b>se / nos</b>: <i>Sentémonos</i> (not sentemosnos), <i>Démoselo</i>."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "pagebreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "2. Redundant pronouns"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        6.0,
        5.6,
        5.4
      ],
      "head": [
        "Spanish",
        "English",
        "Why"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "A mí me gusta el café.",
          "I like coffee.",
          "emphasis / clarity"
        ],
        [
          "A Ana le encantan los gatos.",
          "Ana loves cats.",
          "name + le"
        ],
        [
          "Le di el libro a Ana.",
          "I gave Ana the book.",
          "le is always present"
        ],
        [
          "¿A ti te parece bien?",
          "Does it seem fine to you?",
          "emphasis"
        ],
        [
          "A nosotros nos tocó ganar.",
          "It was our turn to win.",
          "emphasis"
        ],
        [
          "El libro lo compré ayer.",
          "I bought the book yesterday.",
          "topic repeated by lo"
        ],
        [
          "A María la vi ayer.",
          "I saw María yesterday.",
          "topic repeated by la"
        ],
        [
          "Dáselo a ellos.",
          "Give it to them.",
          "clarifies se"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "Rule",
      "text": "If the indirect object appears as a noun, <b>le / les</b> is still required: <i>Escribí a mi madre</i> is possible, but <i>Le escribí a mi madre</i> is more natural. <i>Le di el libro a Ana</i> is the normal order."
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "3. Verbs like gustar"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        4.4,
        6.4,
        6.2
      ],
      "head": [
        "Verb",
        "Example",
        "English"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "encantar",
          "Me encanta el cine.",
          "I love cinema."
        ],
        [
          "importar",
          "No me importa.",
          "I do not mind."
        ],
        [
          "molestar",
          "Me molesta el ruido.",
          "The noise bothers me."
        ],
        [
          "apetecer",
          "¿Te apetece un café?",
          "Do you fancy a coffee?"
        ],
        [
          "parecer",
          "Me parece buena idea.",
          "It seems a good idea to me."
        ],
        [
          "doler",
          "Me duele la cabeza.",
          "My head hurts."
        ],
        [
          "faltar",
          "Me falta tiempo.",
          "I lack time."
        ],
        [
          "sobrar",
          "Nos sobra comida.",
          "We have food left over."
        ],
        [
          "quedar",
          "Me quedan dos euros.",
          "I have two euros left."
        ],
        [
          "hacer falta",
          "Me hace falta ayuda.",
          "I need help."
        ],
        [
          "interesar",
          "Me interesa la política.",
          "Politics interests me."
        ],
        [
          "sorprender",
          "Me sorprende que llegue.",
          "It surprises me that he comes."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The verb agrees with the <b>thing</b> that pleases / hurts / is lacking: <i>Me gustan los libros. Me duelen los pies. Le faltan dos páginas.</i>"
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "4. The neutral lo"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        5.0,
        6.2,
        5.8
      ],
      "head": [
        "Use",
        "Example",
        "English"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "lo + adjective",
          "Lo bueno es que es barato.",
          "The good thing is that it is cheap."
        ],
        [
          "lo + adj. + que",
          "No sabes lo difícil que es.",
          "You do not know how hard it is."
        ],
        [
          "lo que",
          "Lo que dices es verdad.",
          "What you say is true."
        ],
        [
          "lo de",
          "Lo de ayer fue un error.",
          "That thing yesterday was a mistake."
        ],
        [
          "lo + adverb + que",
          "Corre lo más rápido que puede.",
          "He runs as fast as he can."
        ],
        [
          "lo mismo",
          "Quiero lo mismo.",
          "I want the same."
        ],
        [
          "a lo mejor",
          "A lo mejor viene.",
          "Maybe he comes."
        ],
        [
          "por lo menos",
          "Por lo menos llamó.",
          "At least he called."
        ],
        [
          "lo cual",
          "No vino, lo cual me molestó.",
          "He did not come, which annoyed me."
        ],
        [
          "lo + participle",
          "Lo hecho, hecho está.",
          "What is done is done."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "Lo for a whole idea",
      "text": "<b>Lo</b> can replace an idea: <i>¿Está cansado? Sí, lo está.</i> / <i>Lo sé.</i> / <i>No lo creo.</i> After <b>ser, estar, parecer</b> with adjectives it refers to the adjective: <i>Ella es lista y su hermano también lo es.</i>"
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "5. Prepositional and reflexive pronouns"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        4.4,
        4.4,
        4.2,
        4.0
      ],
      "head": [
        "Person",
        "After a preposition",
        "With con",
        "Example"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "yo",
          "mí",
          "conmigo",
          "Es para mí. Ven conmigo."
        ],
        [
          "tú",
          "ti",
          "contigo",
          "Es para ti. Voy contigo."
        ],
        [
          "él / ella / usted",
          "él / ella / usted",
          "con él",
          "Hablo con ella."
        ],
        [
          "reflexive (3rd)",
          "sí",
          "consigo",
          "Lo trajo consigo."
        ],
        [
          "nosotros",
          "nosotros",
          "con nosotros",
          "Vienen con nosotros."
        ],
        [
          "vosotros",
          "vosotros",
          "con vosotros",
          "Voy con vosotros."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "<b>Entre, según, excepto, salvo, menos, incluso</b> take <b>subject</b> pronouns: <i>entre tú y yo, según tú, excepto yo, hasta yo</i>.",
        "<b>Mismo</b> adds emphasis: <i>yo mismo, ella misma, nosotros mismos, por sí mismo</i>.",
        "<b>Uno / una</b> is the general \"one\": <i>Uno nunca sabe.</i>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "6. Leísmo, laísmo and loísmo"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        5.6,
        5.6,
        5.8
      ],
      "head": [
        "Usage",
        "Example",
        "Status"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Standard (Latin America, most of Spain)",
          "A Juan lo vi. A María la vi.",
          "correct"
        ],
        [
          "Leísmo (male people)",
          "A Juan le vi.",
          "accepted in Spain"
        ],
        [
          "Laísmo",
          "A María la di un libro.",
          "not accepted"
        ],
        [
          "Loísmo",
          "A Juan lo di un libro.",
          "not accepted"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "For the indirect object always use <b>le / les</b>: <i>Le di un libro a María.</i> For safe, standard Spanish, use <b>lo</b> for masculine direct objects (<i>Lo vi</i>)."
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "7. Common mistakes"
    },
    {
      "type": "mistakes",
      "rows": [
        [
          "Le lo dije.",
          "Se lo dije.",
          "le + lo: se lo."
        ],
        [
          "Lo me dijo.",
          "Me lo dijo.",
          "indirect before direct."
        ],
        [
          "Quiero decirlo te.",
          "Quiero decírtelo.",
          "indirect first, attached in order."
        ],
        [
          "Me ha lo dicho.",
          "Me lo ha dicho.",
          "pronouns before haber."
        ],
        [
          "Dame lo.",
          "Dámelo.",
          "attached imperative."
        ],
        [
          "Entre tú y mí.",
          "Entre tú y yo.",
          "entre takes subject pronouns."
        ],
        [
          "Voy con mí.",
          "Voy conmigo.",
          "conmigo."
        ],
        [
          "A mí gusta el café.",
          "A mí me gusta el café.",
          "keep me with a mí."
        ],
        [
          "Me gusta los libros.",
          "Me gustan los libros.",
          "gustar agrees with the thing."
        ]
      ]
    },
